	<article>
		
		<div class="primary"><div class="events-container"><div class="events"><h2 class="event-month" id="events-october-2026">October 2026</h2><div class="event filter-shooting-sports"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Wednesday, October 7"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">7</span><span class="event-day-part">Wed</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Archery Fun Shoot</h3><p class="event-locality">Richmond, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>Come join DWR and Freedom Outdoors for a Fun Shoot! Our experienced instructors will be on hand to help with scoring, range etiquette, equipment, safety, and shooting tips. No experience or equipment is required. We will have recurve and Genesis bows available for anyone who needs them, along with the necessary gear. </p>
<p>Come enjoy a fun, relaxed, and welcoming environment while learning the basics of target archery and building your confidence on the range. Archers will have 2 minutes per end to shoot 3 arrows (10 ends total). Genesis archers will be shooting 10m. All other divisions will be shooting 18m. </p>
<p>Warm-up begins at 6:00 pm. Scoring begins at 6:30 pm.</p>
<p>To register through Freedom Outdoors, click the Registration button below. Once on the Freedom Outdoors website, click on the "RVA / DWR Archery" option to select classes/dates.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Freedom Outdoors RVA</li><li class="event-address">6020 W Broad St, Richmond, VA 23230 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=6020+W+Broad+St%2C+Richmond%2C+VA+23230">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/07/2026 (6:30 pm)</li></ul></div><div class="event-fee-container"><h4>Fee</h4><ul class="event-fee"><li>$20.00</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://freedomoutdoors.us/classes-richmond/">Register</a></div></div></div><div class="event filter-shooting-sports"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Saturday, October 10"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">10</span><span class="event-day-part">Sat</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Bowtober Youth and Family Archery Workshop &#8211; Morning</h3><p class="event-locality">Disputanta, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>This two-hour workshop will introduce participants 9 years old and up to the basics of archery through hands-on instruction. All equipment and sullies will be provided. A parent or guardian must stay with any youth participant for the workshop. This is a partnership workshop with the Luck Group and DWR.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Temple Recreation Park</li><li class="event-address">14307 Prince George Dr, Disputanta, VA 23842 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=14307+Prince+George+Dr%2C+Disputanta%2C+VA+23842">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/10/2026 (10:00 am&ndash;12:00 pm)</li></ul></div><div class="event-contact-container"><h4>Contact</h4><ul class="event-contact"><li>Sidney Tyler</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://www.register-ed.com/events/view/248164">Register</a></div></div></div><div class="event filter-shooting-sports"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Saturday, October 10"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">10</span><span class="event-day-part">Sat</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Bowtober Youth and Family Archery Workshop &#8211; Afternoon</h3><p class="event-locality">Disputanta, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>This two-hour workshop will introduce participants 9 years old and up to the basics of archery through hands-on instruction. All equipment and sullies will be provided. A parent or guardian must stay with any youth participant for the workshop. This is a partnership workshop with the Luck Group and DWR.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Temple Recreation Park</li><li class="event-address">14307 Prince George Dr, Disputanta, VA 23842 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=14307+Prince+George+Dr%2C+Disputanta%2C+VA+23842">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/10/2026 (1:00 pm&ndash;3:00 pm)</li></ul></div><div class="event-contact-container"><h4>Contact</h4><ul class="event-contact"><li>Sidney Tyler</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://www.register-ed.com/events/view/248165">Register</a></div></div></div><div class="event filter-hunting filter-virginia-outdoor-women"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Saturday, October 10"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">10</span><span class="event-day-part">Sat</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">VOW/Women&#8217;s Hunter Education Course</h3><p class="event-locality">Stafford, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>This VOW (Virginia Outdoor Women)/Women's Hunter Education Course is offered as a free course to the public. This course is geared toward women and girls ages 11 years old and up. The course is designed to teach you how to become a safe hunter and not how to hunt. Successful completion of the class is required for both youth and first-time hunters to apply for a Virginia Hunting License.</p>
<p>This course requires completion of chapter review questions in the "Today’s Hunter in Virginia" student manual prior to class time. The exercises will be collected by the instructors upon arrival. More details about the chapter exercises and how to acquire a student manual are available on the registration page.</p>
<p>NO LIVE FIREARMS OR AMMUNITION ARE PERMITTED IN THE CLASSROOM. All students 15 years of age or younger MUST be accompanied by a responsible adult for the entire class. Please bring a lunch and read all of the information included in the confirmation email when you register for the class.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Izaak Walton League Stafford</li><li class="event-address">2729 Garrisonville Road, Stafford, VA 22556 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=2729+Garrisonville+Road%2C+Stafford%2C+VA+22556">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/10/2026 (9:00 am&ndash;4:00 pm)</li></ul></div><div class="event-contact-container"><h4>Contact</h4><ul class="event-contact"><li>William G. Roets II</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://www.register-ed.com/events/view/245849">Register</a></div></div></div><div class="event filter-fishing"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Saturday, October 10"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">10</span><span class="event-day-part">Sat</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Trout Fishing Clinic and Stocked Trout Q&#038;A</h3><p class="event-locality">Wytheville, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>DWR hatchery staff will be on hand following the stocking of Wytheville Community College Pond to provide tips and advice to novice anglers and to provide general information about DWR’s Stocked Trout Program.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Wytheville Community College Pond</li><li class="event-address">Community Blvd, Wytheville, VA 24382 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Community+Blvd%2C+Wytheville%2C+VA+24382">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/10/2026 (9:00 am&ndash;11:00 am)</li></ul></div><div class="event-contact-container"><h4>Contact</h4><ul class="event-contact"><li>Butch Bates</li><li>butch.bates@dwr.virginia.gov</li><li>276-637-3212</li></ul></div></div></div></div><div class="event filter-hunting filter-virginia-outdoor-women"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Sunday, October 11"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">11</span><span class="event-day-part">Sun</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Ladies&#8217; Learn to Upland Hunt</h3><p class="event-locality">New Kent, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>Offered by Central Virginia Chapter of Quail Forever, this event is designed for women who are curious about hunting but don’t know where to start. These beginner-friendly experiences offer hands-on instruction in firearm safety, hunting skills, and conservation, all in a supportive, no-pressure environment. </p>
<p>Led by passionate women mentors and guides, you’ll gain confidence in the field, connect with like-minded ladies, and learn how hunting plays a vital role in wildlife and habitat conservation—no experience or gear needed, just a willingness to learn.</p>
<p>Every attendee will receive a one-year membership to Quail Forever, education in conservation and species education, DWR regulations, parlances of the field, bird dog demo, field first aid, gear review and how to clean and prepare your harvest. Open to all women beginners, 16 years and up, current Quail Forever membership not required.  No equipment is required. </p>
<p>VOW Course: This event qualifies as a VOW @ the Field 3, Hunting Workshop (any species/active hunt). This event can be used to complete the Hunting Certification in the Virginia Outdoor Women (VOW) Program. This event is open to all registrants.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Cumberland Estate​​​​​​​​</li><li class="event-address">9007 Cumberland Rd, New Kent, VA 23124 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=9007+Cumberland+Rd%2C+New+Kent%2C+VA+23124">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/11/2026 (8:30 am)</li></ul></div><div class="event-fee-container"><h4>Fee</h4><ul class="event-fee"><li>$150.00</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://quailforever.[long]?slug=ladies-learn-to-upland-hunt">Register</a></div></div></div><div class="event filter-wildlife-education"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Monday, October 12"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">12</span><span class="event-day-part">Mon</span></abbr></span><span class="event-date-through">&ndash;</span><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Tuesday, October 13"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">13</span><span class="event-day-part">Tue</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Upcoming Training Opportunities for Wildlife Control Professionals</h3><p class="event-locality">Henrico, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>The Virginia Wildlife Damage Management Association (VWDMA) provides education and training specifically for wildlife control professionals. This fall, VWDMA will present a Two-Day Fall Wildlife Control Training Series at the Virginia Tech Richmond Center featuring the VWDMA Fall Conference on October 12 and NWCOA Bat Standards Part I on October 13.</p>
<p>Both programs offer valuable professional development for Virginia WCOs, including CNAP continuing education opportunities. The Bat Standards Part I course also satisfies the additional bat management training and testing requirement for those providing bat management services in Virginia.</p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Virginia Tech Richmond Center</li><li class="event-address">2810 N. Parham Rd Suite 300, Henrico, VA 23294 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=2810+N.+Parham+Rd+Suite+300%2C+Henrico%2C+VA+23294">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/12/2026 (9:00 am&ndash;5:00 pm)</li><li class="event-schedule-date">10/13/2026 (9:30 am&ndash;4:30 pm)</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://associationdatabase.com/aws/VWDMA/pt/sp/events">More Information</a></div></div></div><div class="event filter-hunting filter-virginia-outdoor-women"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Saturday, October 17"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">17</span><span class="event-day-part">Sat</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Virginia Trapper Education Course</h3><p class="event-locality">Bland, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>This will be an opportunity to learn the art of trapping. We will provide you with the basic knowledge of trapping in Virginia. You will learn a lot in the time spent in class and in the field. Please dress for the weather, rain or shine. We will set some traps in the dirt. Please bring your lunch and water. </p>
</div><div class="event-metadata"><div class="event-location-container"><h4>Location</h4><ul class="event-location"><li class="event-location-name">Bland County Fairgrounds</li><li class="event-address">117 Fairgrounds Street, Bland, VA 24315 (<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=117+Fairgrounds+Street%2C+Bland%2C+VA+24315">map</a>)</li></ul></div><div class="event-schedule-container"><h4>Event Schedule</h4><ul class="event-schedule"><li class="event-schedule-date">10/17/2026 (8:00 am&ndash;3:00 pm)</li></ul></div><div class="event-contact-container"><h4>Contact</h4><ul class="event-contact"><li>Craig M. Kunkel</li></ul></div></div><div class="event-links-container"><a class="button cta" href="https://www.register-ed.com/events/view/248156">Register</a></div></div></div><div class="event"><div class="event-date-container"><p class="event-date"><span class="event-start-date"><abbr title="Monday, October 19"><span class="event-month-part">Oct</span><span class="event-date-part">19</span><span class="event-day-part">Mon</span></abbr></span></p></div><div class="event-data-container"><h3 class="event-title">Lancaster County Hunter-Landowner Meeting &#8211; Change of Date/Location</h3><p class="event-locality">Lancaster, VA</p><div class="event-description"><p>The purpose of the newly introduced Lancaster County Hunter-Landowner meetings is to provide a productive opportunity for hunters, private landowners, law enforcement, and other community stakeholders to positively collaborate with a local focus. Meeting goals include enhancing communication, building positive relationships, addressing concerns, and working together to develop solutions that will benefit the community. A conversation will be held on the benefits of establishing a local hunter/landowner committee in Lancaster County.</p>
